# QEMU redeploy: monitor → fix → restart → commit

When bringing up or refreshing the Korus QEMU stack (server API `:18080`, web UI `:19088`):

## Cycle (repeat until green or blocked)

1. **Monitor** — before and during every redeploy:
   - `Test-KorusQemuStackRunning` (VM PIDs alive)
   - `http://127.0.0.1:18080/api/v1/health` and `/ready`
   - `http://127.0.0.1:19088/`
   - `deploy/qemu/run/*-serial.log`, `redeploy-monitored.log`, guest `/var/log/korus-bootstrap.log` (via plink)
2. **Diagnose** on error or hang (>20 min no progress, VM died, plink abort, stale lock):
   - Stale `qemu-redeploy-*.lock` when stack down or age ≥45m → remove
   - VM died mid-wait → `qemu-up -KeepDisks`, do not blind-wait HTTP
   - `Software caused connection abort` → retry plink (`Update-KorusGuestRepo`); if VM dead, restart VMs first
   - False `[OK] web` without expected assets → redeploy web or enable hotswap
3. **Fix** — minimal diff in scripts/lib; no host Docker
4. **Restart** — `.\scripts\qemu-redeploy-monitored.ps1` (preferred) or `qemu-up -KeepDisks` then `qemu-redeploy.ps1 -ServerOnly` / `-WebOnly`
   - Script sets `golden-path.no-auto-restart` (blocks `qemu-auto-restart` from minute-status)
   - After fresh `qemu-up`: wait SSH 12221/12222 + 90s settle before redeploy
5. **Commit** — after each fix+restart cycle that changes repo files (user-requested pattern); message: what broke and what fixed

## Preferred entrypoints

```powershell
.\scripts\qemu-up.ps1 -KeepDisks
.\scripts\qemu-redeploy-monitored.ps1 -Target server    # API up (~20-25 min)
.\scripts\qemu-redeploy-monitored.ps1 -Target web       # UI up
.\scripts\qemu-redeploy-monitored.ps1 -Target both -EnableHotswap
```

## Constraints

- **Never** `qemu-down` without user request
- **Never** kill non-Korus `qemu-system-x86_64`
- Runtime only in QEMU guests (see `qemu-host-isolation.mdc`)
- Report status in Russian: VM alive?, API code, UI code, last log line, next action
